hey everyone jake here we're going to  have a lot of destiny 2 content in the  near future so if you want to stay up to  date make sure to subscribe to our  channel  thank you and enjoy  if there's a single word to describe  destiny 2 it's disruption  in the sequel to bungie's popular shared  world shooter the guardians of earth  have finally met their match with a new  villain who's got his eyes on the  traveler  with their powers stripped away and all  their gear destroyed our heroes are  pushed back to square one and they have  to relearn what it means to be a true  guardian of the light  is mine  though it'll be sad to see our valuable  exotics fade into the ether this turns  out to be a blessing as our next  adventure for our characters will bring  new challenges new rewards and an even  greater feeling of satisfaction when  accomplishing the next big battle  though the general grind in destiny 2 is  the same there are a number of big  differences this time around and  gamespot is here to let you know  some of the bigger changes since the  last game's adventure  [Music]  while destiny 1's narrative was  undoubtedly built on a universe with a  vast history and a lot of thought put  into it it often struggled with  conveying those ideas  opting for a more fragmented and  episodic take on its storytelling with  the sequel bungie has gone with a  traditional approach for a more  consistent narrative  gradually fleshing out key characters in  locales and giving them the moments they  deserve  impressing uk is the easiest thing i'll  do all day  teasing the taking king mission outbound  signal the main antagonist in destiny 2  is cabal emperor dominus gaul  unlike the first game which struggled to  figure out exactly what the darkness was  the warlord behind the red legion is a  tangible character with additional story  beats revealing why he came to earth to  find the traveler and what his plans are  with its power  if you're a returning guardian this  story will essentially pick up where you  left off after rise of iron  destiny went through several loot  overhauls over its first year and beyond  making great strides in the taking king  expansion before it found a sense of  equilibrium  in destiny 2 the loot system has been  revised a bit more  focusing more on keeping players in the  action better gear comes in a more  steady stream  and generally won't come encrypted  enabling guardians to stay powered up  while preventing the hassle of dragging  encrypted engrams to the crypt arc  moreover random roles for weapons and  armor have been dropped ditching the  frustration of finding rare weapons with  lousy perks  there are also more opportunities and  ways to find new gear with high profile  targets that drop loot cases  the lost sectors and finishing tasks for  each planet's faction to yield rewards  when unlocking loot you'll no longer  have to undergo bizarre rituals to  ensure that you get the best  outcome overall gear power in your  entire inventory will be factored in  making switching over to your most  powerful gear unnecessary  furthermore encrypted engrams are more  rare and allowing a maximum of 10  encrypted engrams to be held at any  given time  when it comes to exploration destiny 2  will make much better use of your time  in the open areas on each planet  while the drop destiny 1 was about the  exploration of planets and interstellar  locales  it often felt limited in scope with its  focus of repeating daily missions and  patrols  with places like the european dead zone  the largest map in a destiny game  the new diversions and opportunities  make the various locations feel much  more fleshed out  with public quests and other activities  shown clearly on the map along with  timers for upcoming events and rally  flags to summon guardians there's much  less busy work when trying to figure out  what to do  next while there's still plenty of  patrol and story missions taking you  around various game worlds the new  adventure missions are more directed  quests given out by allies in the field  focusing on the history of the planet  they'll send you to the more obscure and  bizarre reaches of the world while  learning more of the setting and the  characters that inhabit it  is that a sack full of shanks  what do you think they're going to do  with all that tech can you make a big  shank from a bunch of little shanks  these missions offer a nice break from  the more epic and set-piece-focused  story missions and the plain objectives  of patrols while also getting to learn  more about the allies that still inhabit  the spaces  [Music]  though the original game had various  shaders ships sparrows and unique pieces  of class armor to unlock it felt  rudimentary  making the sight of a similar guardian a  common occurrence  the sequel will offer more variation and  change up the number of systems that  made the accessories and options feel  constrained  on top of this the eververse will have  more use aside from being the designated  microtransaction  shop with the new bright engrams these  special lootcases yield a variety of  standard and cosmetic gameplay items  including  shaders which are now consumables  applied to single pieces of gear and  brand new ships for your guardian  found throughout the quests and after  reaching level 20 with each level up  after granting a new engram  these offer more dedicated ways to  acquire new accessories  along with new items called auras a  dedicated option for visual effects such  as flames and other odd designs applied  to your characters cosmetics now come in  a variety of  tiers we acquired an exotic ranked emote  from a bright engram which allowed the  guardian to channel their powers to  express themselves in some odd and  amusing  ways there are ways to customize your  loadouts as well  in addition to the various shaders new  weapons mods can be found and applied to  your weapons  in addition to this is the return of  infusing which is more viable than it is  in the previous game  [Music]  while the destiny community are  resilient for keeping up with the game  there were a distinct lack of systems to  support them in the long run  several websites were created by fans to  fill in the gap for tracking public  events  clan support and several looking for  group databases  bungie have now made great strides with  integrating these features into the game  matchmaking is now available for  high-end content for solo players who  will be paired up with clans and other  fire teams looking for members  there is now also dedicated clan support  giving players the chance to create a  group on bungie's official site and  invite members of the community to join  along with creating unique clan banners  and having clan dedicated chats and  forums a clan will also work together to  gain unique clan rewards and bonuses  through their journey which are  cumulatively added up among members  these rewards come in many different  forms such as unique emblems and auras  but will constantly change and shift  depending on the weekly refresh  for those returning destiny 2 will be an  experience that is familiar but also  more refined  and detailed in its approach to building  up a unique character  and for those coming in fresh bungie's  sequel looks to offer a stunning  and broad game world to explore along  with tons of monsters to shoot and loot  to find  this shared world shooter has a lot on  display and after years of work it's  ready to show off what it can do in its  second outing  if you're craving more destiny 2 content  be on the lookout for our upcoming show  destiny's children where our us and uk  teams will take the reins on long plays  and live streams for destiny 2.  thank you for watching  [Music]  this is great anyone want a hug no hugs
 

